{title: 60 Years}
{artist: Elton John}
{key: B}

{c: Verse 1}
[B] [A],        Wholl walk me down to church
[G] [F#],        when Im sixty years of age
[Em],        When the ragged dog they gave me
[F#],        has been ten years in the grave
[B] [A],        And senorita play guitar,
[G] [F#],        play it just for you
[Em],        My rosary has broken and
[F#] [B],        my beads have all slipped through
[B] [A],        Youve hung up your great coat
[G] [F#],        and youve laid down your gun
[Em],        You know the war you fought
[F#],        in wasnt too much fun
[B] [A],        And the future youre giving me
[G] [F#],        holds nothing for a gun
[Em] [F#],        Ive no wish to be living sixty years on
[B] [A],        Yes Ill sit with you and talk
[G] [F#],        let your eyes relive again
[Em],        I know my vintage prayers
[F#],        would be very much the same
[B] [A],        And Magdelena plays the organ,
[G] [F#],        plays it just for you
[Em],        Your choral lamp that burns so low
[F#],        when you are passing through
[B] [A],        And the future youre giving me
[G] [F#],        holds nothing for a gun
[B] [A] [B],        Ive no wish to be living sixty years on
